  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ISF Somalia: Women to women security &#x2013; phase II (2025&#x2013;27)ISF Somalia: Women to women security &#x2013; phase II (2025&#x2013;27)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Funded by the UK&apos;s Integrated Security Fund (ISF), the project aims to enhance the security of Somali women, girls, and minority groups by facilitating their meaningful inclusion in local decision-making on peace and security. Building upon the successful Women to Women (W2W) Security Pilot Project, this initiative will employ horizontal and vertical dialogues, a micro-grant mechanism, and targeted capacity building to empower women and promote their participation in security governance. It also includes strategic engagement with men and boys to foster support for gender equality and social inclusion within Somali communities. This project aligns with broader UK initiatives in Somalia, contributing to community safety and resilience across multiple regions, including potential interventions in Newly and Recently Recovered Areas (NRRAs).</narrative>
  </description>
